        en: { name: 'San Francisco convent bell tower', description: 'The yellow bell tower of a former Franciscan convent is Trinidad’s most recognisable landmark. From the top you see tiled roofs, the Escambray Mountains and the sea on the horizon.', tip: 'Climb up close to sunset, when the light turns golden and the roofs and the Plaza Mayor church line up like a postcard.' },
