        en: { name: 'La Canchánchara tavern', description: 'An old tavern in a colonial house with a patio, serving the namesake drink of the independence fighters: rum with honey and lime in clay cups. A live son band is almost always playing.', tip: 'Come in the afternoon, when the musicians are already playing and it is less crowded, and take your clay cup home as a souvenir.' },
